pull":true}},"body":"<!-- Before reporting: search existing issues and check the FAQ. -->\r\n\r\n- `nvim --version`: xterm-256color\r\n- Vim (version: ) behaves differently? Yes\r\n- Operating system/version: macOS 10.13\r\n- Terminal name/version: Terminal.app\r\n- `$TERM`:\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce using `nvim -u NORC`\r\n\r\n```\r\nnvim -u NORC\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Actual behaviour\r\n\r\nstatusline middle area is blank. This is similar to https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/9282 , but in that case it required CTRL-L, and I was running inside tmux. In this case, running in Terminal.app outside of tmux, the behavior is consistent, and CTRL-L doesn't change anything. (I didn't notice this before because I normally am always inside tmux.)\r\n\r\n![nvim-blank-statusline](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1359421/49766697-4e338400-fcd6-11e8-95ff-bb344e5d45a4.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Expected behaviour\r\n\r\nstatusline should paint with the StatusLine background color.\r\n\r\ncc @bfredl ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/9346/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/9346/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]